te_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03422450630060015,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":49.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.025534565082001245,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":57.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.03568,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":23.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Brookfield Asset Management Ltd. is a private equity firm specializing in acquisitions and growth capital investments. The firm primarily provides its services to institutional clients, high net worth individuals, financial institutions, public and private pension plans, sovereign wealth funds, endowments, and foundations. The firm manages separate client-focused public and private fund portfolios, listed partnerships, separate accounts, and co-investments. The firm invests in real assets, including real estate, infrastructure, renewable power, private equity, and credit. The firm employs fundamental and operational analysis to make its investments. The firm uses both in-house and external research to complement its investment process. Brookfield Asset Management Ltd. was founded in 2022 and is based in New York. Brookfield Asset Management Ltd. operates as a subsidiary of Brookfield Corporation.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James Bruce Flatt | Chair, Affiliated Director & CEO of Brookfield Corporation | Age 60 | Compensation: $375,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $831K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $361K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $21K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Brookfield Asset Management Inc is a large-cap financial services business with a $82.3B market cap on $4.8B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 47% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 36-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $2.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 43 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.88\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 35\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 67% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6662275812168404},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 33% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Brookfield Asset Management (NYSE:BAM) Stock Price Target Raised at Wells Fargo & Company","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/brookfield-asset-management-nysebam-stock-price-target-raised-at-wells-fargo-company.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794587457.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Bloom Energy vs. Constellation Energy: On-Site Power or Grid Power, Which Wins the Data Center?","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/11/13/bloom-energy-vs-constellation-energy-on-site-power/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794559560.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.711,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Jensen Huang Is Out as Nvidia CEO. Could These 3 Industrial Stocks Pay the Price?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/jensen-huang-nvidia-ceo-could-215003000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794520877.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.382,